{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a5340fc763cabe30675ff70692b4c9d3e170a4fc678a65eb6df1ad770d2e30c0","digest":{"component_or_area":"git fetch timeout handling","key_entities":["rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.stall_abort_args()","rebar._snapshot.git_fetch.is_stall_abort()","review_bot/gerrit_client.py:367,401","opcert_service/workspace.py:107,124","_commands/init.py:398,419","_commands/_init_probe.run_bounded_git","_GIT_TIMEOUT","_FETCH_TIMEOUT","http.lowSpeedLimit","http.lowSpeedTime"],"problem_keywords":["git timeout","throughput stall detection","low-speed abort","network fetch"],"propositions":["Three remaining 300s git fetch call sites expose the same throughput stall vulnerability as the snapshot path fixed in 12e4","The gerrit_client, opcert_service, and init command fetch operations currently use only wall-clock timeout without low-speed abort, causing byte-starved transfers to burn the full 300s instead of aborting in ~10s","Each of the three sites must splice stall_abort_args() into its git subcommand argv to reuse the low-speed abort mechanism without duplicating logic","A stalled remote (zero-byte after headers) must abort on throughput, while a dribbling remote above the low-speed floor must not be aborted as a stall"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787642211571716001,"uuid":"bc430614-a454-43a2-b95b-d6f36f416c2e"}